🔐 JWT Security API Flow

Your APIs are:

#	Method	API	JWT
| # | Method | API              | JWT    |
| - | ------ | ---------------- | -----  |
| 1 | POST   | `/auth/register` | ❌ No  |
| 2 | POST   | `/auth/login`    | ❌ No  |
| 3 | GET    | `/user/hello`    | ✅ Yes |
| 4 | GET    | `/user/profile`  | ✅ Yes |


Base URL:

http://localhost:8080
1️⃣ Register User
API
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Authorization
No Auth
Body

Select:

Body
→ raw
→ JSON

Send:

{
    "username": "Raj",
    "email": "raj@gmail.com",
    "password": "12345"
}
Response
User registered successfully
What happens internally?
Postman
   ↓
/auth/register
   ↓
AuthController
   ↓
AuthService
   ↓
Check email
   ↓
existsByEmail()
   ↓
BCrypt encrypt password
   ↓
UserRepository
   ↓
MySQL

Your database will contain something like:

id | username | email         | password
------------------------------------------------
1  | Raj      | raj@gmail.com | $2a$10$......

⚠️ The password is not stored as 12345. BCrypt encrypts it.

2️⃣ Login

After registration, login.

API
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login?email=raj@gmail.com&password=12345
Authorization
No Auth
Body

No body required.

Response

You will receive a long string:

eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJyYWpAZ21haWwuY29tIiwiaWF0Ijox...

This is your JWT token.

🔑 What happens during Login?
Postman
   ↓
POST /auth/login
   ↓
AuthController
   ↓
AuthService
   ↓
AuthenticationManager
   ↓
CustomUserDetailsService
   ↓
UserRepository
   ↓
Find user by email
   ↓
BCrypt checks password
   ↓
Password correct
   ↓
JwtService
   ↓
Generate JWT
   ↓
Return JWT to Postman
3️⃣ Copy JWT Token

Copy the complete token returned from login.

Example:

eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJyYWpAZ21haWwuY29tIiwiaWF0Ijox...

Keep it.

You will use it for protected APIs.

4️⃣ Test Protected API Without JWT

Now test:

GET http://localhost:8080/user/hello
Authorization
No Auth
Expected response
401 Unauthorized

This proves that the API is protected.

5️⃣ Test /user/hello With JWT

Now:

GET http://localhost:8080/user/hello

Go to:

Authorization
→ Type: Bearer Token

Paste your JWT:

eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9....

Postman automatically sends:

Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9....
Response
Hello raj@gmail.com, you are authenticated using JWT!
